# =============================================================================
# Trivy ignore list
# =============================================================================
# Every entry here MUST carry a justification and a removal condition. An
# unexplained ignore is indistinguishable from an unnoticed vulnerability.
# Re-check this file whenever `Security Scan` newly passes — an entry that no
# longer matches anything should be deleted, not left to rot.

# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — react-router "RSC Mode CSRF Bypass Allows Action
# Execution Before 400 Response" (HIGH). Installed 7.18.1; fixed in 8.3.0.
#
# Not exploitable in this application. The advisory is specific to React
# Server Components mode. This frontend is a client-only Vite SPA:
#   - src/main.tsx mounts <BrowserRouter>, not a data/RSC router
#   - no SSR entrypoint (no entry.server.*, no server.*)
#   - no @react-router/* server packages in frontend/package.json
#   - no createStaticHandler / renderToPipeableStream anywhere in src/
# There is no server-side action pipeline for the bypass to act on.
#
# The fix requires react-router-dom 7.x -> 8.3.0, a major upgrade across 25+
# dashboard routes. That is tracked as planned work rather than rushed in
# under an advisory that does not apply here — the migration's regression
# surface is materially larger than this exposure.
#
# REMOVE THIS ENTRY when react-router-dom reaches >= 8.3.0.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Container image scan — pip's own vendored/bundled artifacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The two entries below are NOT application dependencies. They live inside
# pip's private trees in the backend image and are never imported by app code.
# Confirmed by inspecting the built image directly:
#
#   /usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pip/_vendor/msgpack
#   /usr/local/lib/python3.11/ensurepip/_bundled/setuptools-79.0.1-py3-none-any.whl
#   /usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/setuptools-83.0.0.dist-info  <- real one
#
# Ignored per-advisory rather than via --skip-dirs on the vendor trees: a
# genuine vulnerability in a vendored package would still surface, instead of
# whole directories silently dropping out of the scan.

# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 — msgpack "Out-of-bounds read / crash on Unpacker reuse
# after a caught error" (HIGH). Reported against 1.1.2, fixed in 1.2.1.
#
# Not an installed dependency. The only copy is pip's vendored one under
# site-packages/pip/_vendor/msgpack, which pip uses internally for its HTTP
# cache. Nothing in app/ imports msgpack, and it is absent from requirements.
# It is only upgradeable by pip itself re-vendoring, not by us.
#
# REMOVE THIS ENTRY if msgpack ever becomes a real dependency (add it to
# requirements at >= 1.2.1 at that point), or once pip vendors >= 1.2.1.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# CVE-2025-47273 — setuptools "Path Traversal in PackageIndex" (HIGH). Fixed
# in 78.1.1.
#
# The image's actual setuptools is 83.0.0 — the Dockerfile already upgrades
# pip/setuptools/wheel before installing requirements, specifically citing
# this CVE. The finding comes from the wheel bundled inside ensurepip, which
# is only used to seed new virtualenvs and is never installed at runtime; the
# image creates no venv. That bundled copy is 79.0.1, itself already past the
# 78.1.1 fix.
#
# REMOVE THIS ENTRY once the python:3.11-slim-bookworm base ships an ensurepip
# bundle Trivy no longer flags.
CVE-2025-47273
